4 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 5 0 R
  /Title (1.1 In your previous projects, you built applications with JavaScript, TypeScript, React, PHP, databases, and frameworks. You also already experienced teamwork and Scrum in a first simulation. This project is the end-year milestone, the technical challenge is real, but the main objective is to deliver software as a team.)
  /Dest 487 0 R
>>
endobj

5 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 6 0 R
  /Prev 4 0 R
  /Title (1.2 You will work in a team of 4 to 6 apprentices. Your team will probably include people with different levels of experience: not everyone will have completed exactly the same previous projects. This is intentional. In professional teams, you rarely work only with people who know exactly the same things as you. You will need to share knowledge, distribute work fairly, review each other's code, and make sure the whole team can understand the product.)
  /Dest 488 0 R
>>
endobj

6 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 7 0 R
  /Prev 5 0 R
  /Title (1.3 The technology stack is fixed: you will build a web application with Laravel. This constraint is here to reduce time lost on technology choices and to let you focus on collaboration, delivery, product quality, and Scrum practice. You are expected to use Laravel conventions, Blade, Eloquent, migrations, validation, authorization.)
  /Dest 489 0 R
>>
endobj

7 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 8 0 R
  /Prev 6 0 R
  /Title (1.4 The concrete product idea is not described in this brief. Your trainer will play the stakeholder/client role and will reveal the business need during the first stakeholder meeting. Your team must contact the stakeholder at the start of the project and schedule this first meeting, as in a real professional mandate.)
  /Dest 490 0 R
>>
endobj

8 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 9 0 R
  /Prev 7 0 R
  /Title (1.5 Your team will use Scrum with three-day sprints. The team chooses who starts as Product Owner, Scrum Master, and Developers. Roles rotate every two sprints so that several apprentices practise coordination, backlog ownership, facilitation, and implementation responsibilities.)
  /Dest 491 0 R
>>
endobj

9 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Prev 8 0 R
  /Title (1.6 Each sprint must produce a demonstrable increment. At the end of every sprint, you present what works to the stakeholder and collect feedback. Every two sprints, when roles change, the team runs a retrospective and chooses concrete improvement actions for the next cycle.)
  /Dest 492 0 R
>>
endobj

